# Update the Changelog

When making changes that will eventually be committed and pushed, update `CHANGELOG.md` in the same change set.

## Requirements

- Add an entry for user-facing and notable internal changes before committing/pushing.
- Skip trivial-only edits (typos, formatting-only, comment-only) unless they are the whole change being shipped.
- Keep entries concise and written for humans reading the project history.

## Format

Match the existing style in `CHANGELOG.md`:

- Group entries under a `## YYYY-MM-DD` heading for today's date.
- If today's date heading already exists, append bullets under it.
- If it does not exist, add a new heading at the top (below `# Changelog`).
- Use a short imperative or descriptive bullet per change.

```markdown
## 2026-08-25

- Replace the family page “Lock” text with a lock icon, and show a “Logout” tooltip on hover.
- Make the family page URL clickable on admin, with a clipboard copy control.
```

## Checklist before push

- [ ] `CHANGELOG.md` includes an entry for this change under today's date
- [ ] The changelog update is included in the commit being pushed
